{"id":"3d13990f-613b-46dd-bb81-1abed97ea4aa","object":"chat.completion","created":1793337191,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Config factory + new config item in `environ.py`:\n\n```python\nr1 = replace_text(\"deepinfer/environ.py\",\n'''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n''',\n'''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def optional_int(*, minimum: int | None = None) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        \"\"\"Parse an optional int env var, optionally requiring a lower bound.\"\"\"\n\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            value = int(v)\n            if minimum is not None and value < minimum:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{value}, must be >= {minimum}\")\n            return value\n\n        return EnvVar(_init)\n''',\n\"fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\")\nprint(r1[\"file_hash\"])\nr2 = replace_text(\"deepinfer/environ.py\",\n'''    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n''',\n'''    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.optional_int(minimum=32)\n    \"普通诊断日志消息正文的最大字符数；未设置（None）表示不限长，统计日志始终完整输出。\"\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n''',\nr1[\"file_hash\"])\nprint(r2[\"file_hash\"])\n```","reasoning_content":"I've read environ.py fully already (registered). I read parts. I need to see the logger.py full class and init—seen. stats_logger worker—seen.\n\nNow apply edits. First environ.py: add a config factory method for optional int with min value. Requirements:\n- unset → None\n- set → int parse, must >=32; empty string, unparsable, or <32 raise ValueError; error text must contain variable name (descriptor wraps with name already). But empty string: int(\"\") raises ValueError whose message \"invalid literal...\" then wrapped with name. OK. But must raise ValueError specifically. int(\"\") raises ValueError. Good.\n- Cache via descriptor: adding class attribute of EnvVar works.\n- rearm single/all works via _descriptors registration; __set_name__ registers.\n\nAdd factory method `int_or_none_min` or helper `_optional_min_int`. Better add static method:\n\n```python\n    @staticmethod\n    def optional_int(*, minimum: int | None = None) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            value = int(v)\n            if minimum is not None and value < minimum:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{value}, must be >= {minimum}\")\n            return value\n        return EnvVar(_init)\n```\n\nThen in class Logging section:\n```python\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.optional_int(minimum=32)\n```\n\nNote empty string int(\"\") raises ValueError → wrapped with name. Good.\n\nNaming: maybe tests call rearm(\"DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\"). Works.\n\nlogger.py: extend NewLineFormatter with keyword-only max_message_chars. Validate: int >= 32, bool not int, else ValueError. Also `None` allowed. Signature: keep four positional params, new param keyword-only:\n\n```python\n    def __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars=None):\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= 32 or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n            if max_message_chars < 32:\n                raise ValueError(...)\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nFormat: need to replace args first, compute on record message, then truncate without mutating record. super().format(record) computes record.message via getMessage and formats. Approach: compute message = record.getMessage() first; if truncation needed, temporarily set record.msg to truncated and args to () during super().format, then restore. But requirement \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\" — temporarily modifying is risky with concurrency; better create copy of record? Use `logging.makeLogRecord`? Simplest safe: build formatted text using super().format on a shallow copy with copy.copy? But formatting includes exception text etc. Use `copy.copy(record)`? Actually logging.LogRecord attributes; copy.copy copies __dict__ shallow — fine. But exception info may need... copy retains references.\n\nAlternative: compute prefix manually? Better: create a copy via `logging.LogRecord(...)`? Simpler: use `record_copy = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)` — makeLogRecord(dict) creates LogRecord with attributes updated; message may be present in dict (record.message set after formatting). Fine.\n\nBut tests may check that shared record's msg, args unchanged. Copy approach safe.\n\nRequirement order: \"先完成 %s 等参数替换，再计算消息长度。预算只限制消息正文，不包含时间、级别等前缀、异常回溯或 stack_info\". So compute record.getMessage(), truncate if len exceeds, then format with truncated message while retaining exc_info/stack_info.\n\nImplementation:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        if self.max_message_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n            return self._format_with_multiline(record)\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        if len(message) <= self.max_message_chars:\n            return self._format_with_multiline(record)\n        truncated = _truncate_message(message, self.max_message_chars)\n        clone = logging.makeLogRecord(dict(record.__dict__))\n        clone.msg = truncated\n        clone.args = ()\n        clone.message = truncated\n        return self._format_with_multiline(clone)\n```\n\nWait: makeLogRecord copies exc_info etc. But `record.message` may exist leading to getMessage returning msg % args when args empty → if msg is plain string, fine; if original msg was format string with args, we've replaced. However makeLogRecord's args set to () and message attr set; logging.Formatter.format calls record.getMessage() which does `msg = str(self.msg); if self.args: msg = msg % self.args` — args empty → fine.\n\nBut `logging.makeLogRecord` with dict containing 'message' sets attribute; ok.\n\nAlso keep_full_message check: exact `is True`. `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True` — but if absent, None is not True. Good.\n\nMultiline prefix logic uses `record.message` — previously in `format` it referenced record.message (set by super().format). In helper, after super().format, record.message set. But for clone we set message beforehand; super().format will recompute and set message. Fine.\n\nHelper `_format_impl`:\n\n```python\n    def _format_record(self, record):\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(record.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n            if color:\n                msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n        return msg\n```\n\nTruncation function module-level:\n\n```python\n_OMIT_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\ndef _truncate_message(message: str, max_chars: int) -> str:\n    budget = max_chars - len(_OMIT_MARKER)\n    head_len = (budget + 1) // 2\n    tail_len = budget - head_len\n    return message[:head_len] + _OMIT_MARKER + (message[len(message) - tail_len:] if tail_len else \"\")\n```\n\nCheck budget: max 32, marker len 15 → budget 17 → head 9, tail 8. Matches example. If max_chars=32 exactly, budget 17. Good. For max_chars >= 32 budget >=17 positive.\n\nEdge: message length > max; budget < len(message). Fine. tail slice: message[-tail_len:] better for tail_len 0 → message[-0:] = whole string! Use message[len(message)-tail_len:].\n\nNow default init: `_setup_logger` pass `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`. Need import: `from deepinfer.environ import envs`. Check logger.py uses no environ import. Add import. Careful circular import: environ imports nothing from logger. Fine.\n\nEach `_setup_logger` creates new formatter with current cached config; repeated init doesn't add handler (already guarded). Good.\n\nstats_logger: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nLet me apply environ edit first. Need to confirm the exact text around Logging section for replace. Use old text:\n\n```\n    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n```\nand add new line. Also add factory method after int_or_none.\n\nLet's do both replace_text on same file—each checks hash; after first edit hash changes. Do sequentially with returned hash."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9463,"completion_tokens":2163,"total_tokens":11626,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3968},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1754},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":3968,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":5495},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}